## SQ-MELT-05 | Nether: ice beside a Salt Block -> air, never water
@group B-nether
@commands In the Nether (forceloaded): `ice` beside a Salt Block, a control ice without salt; wait 120 s at randomTickSpeed 1000
@pass ice -> air (never water)
@fails `meltedState` ultra-warm check; Immersive Weathering also melts Nether ice by itself (expected, [melting.md](../melting.md) 6)
@from batches/r1115/p3_a1.qb
# self-contained since r1118 R2 (2026-11-18): setup and build from r1115 p3_a1.qb P3-00 / P3-01 (not migrated);
# bot m3n on a stone platform on the Nether roof keeps it random-ticking; the retired zmelt probe is not used
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run forceload add 0 0 31 31
> gamerule doFireTick false
> gamerule doMobSpawning false
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run fill 0 128 0 31 128 31 minecraft:stone
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run fill 0 129 0 31 133 31 minecraft:air
sleep 3
> execute unless entity m3n run pbot spawn m3n 8 129 8 minecraft:the_nether survival
sleep 3
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run setblock 5 129 4 minecraft:ice
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run setblock 4 129 4 salt:salt_block
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run setblock 20 129 20 minecraft:ice
sleep 1
reject (Unknown (item|block|block type|entity)|Incorrect argument for command|Unknown or incomplete command|Block property)
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 1000
sleep 120
> gamerule randomTickSpeed 3
> execute in minecraft:the_nether if block 5 129 4 minecraft:air run say SQ-MELT-05-ice_air
expect SQ-MELT-05-ice_air$
look ice beside the salt went to air (never water: a water source would stay); the control ice 20 129 20 (no salt) state is recorded for Immersive Weathering's own Nether melt
> execute in minecraft:the_nether run cdevtest state 20 129 20
reject \[cdevtest\] .*done=0

## SQ-MELT-06 | part 1 (switch off): torch, soul torch, lantern, sconce, copper lantern, glowstone melt at 3, not 4; sea lantern, redstone torch, jelly torch, unlit brazier nothing
@group A
@commands Ice at distance 3 and at distance 4 from each of: `torch`, `soul_torch`, `lantern`, `supplementaries:sconce`, `everythingcopper:copper_lantern`, `glowstone`; ice touching each of `sea_lantern`, `redstone_torch`, `upgrade_aquatic:blue_jelly_torch`; ice 1 from `decorative_blocks:brazier[lit=false]`; wait 90 s. Then `qrun.py toml creativecompat-common.toml melting vanillaLightMelting true`, restart, ice touching a sea lantern again, wait 90 s
@pass distance 3 melted, 4 not, for all six; sea lantern, redstone torch, jelly torch and unlit brazier ice unchanged; with the switch on the sea-lantern ice melts
@fails a modded id missing from the tag: `melting_tags.js` globs / `has()`; sea lantern melting with the switch off: `VanillaLightMeltMixin` not applied (grep `latest.log` for the mixin)
@from batches/r1115/p3_a1.qb
