@commands in the End place a torch-lit fire block (`setblock ~ ~ ~ minecraft:fire`) and flint-and-steel it with a bot; then `qrun.py toml config/creativecompat-common.toml melting endNoFire false` and repeat
@pass endNoFire true: no fire in the End and no sound; false: fire is placed; latest.log has no `EndFireMixin` apply error
@fails `EndFireMixin` is in Compat's `mixin/`, listed in `MixinSwitches` as `EndFireMixin` (toml key `[mixins] endFire`, `MixinSwitches.key`: the name without `Mixin`, first letter lower case); a false `endFire` skips it; `Melting.onScheduledTick` removal of fire already there
@reviewed 2026-11-25
@modset none
# r1124gate (2026-11-24, runner-4): End void spot x 200 to 215, z 200 to 215, y 64 (clear of the main island); the
# setblock refusal reads "Could not set the block"; cdevtest use = a fake player of the End with flint and steel.
# endNoFire is set by a restart each way so the row does not depend on SQ-MELT-21/-22's carried values.
bootreject (?i)^(?=.*EndFireMixin).*(apply failed|InvalidInjection|exception|could not)
edit python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py" toml config/creativecompat-common.toml melting endNoFire true
restart
> execute in minecraft:the_end run forceload add 200 200 215 215
sleep 5
> execute in minecraft:the_end run fill 200 63 200 215 63 215 minecraft:end_stone
> execute in minecraft:the_end run setblock 210 63 210 minecraft:soul_soil
> execute in minecraft:the_end run setblock 204 64 204 minecraft:fire
> execute in minecraft:the_end run setblock 210 64 210 minecraft:soul_fire
> cdevtest use 206 63 206 held=minecraft:flint_and_steel face=up dim=minecraft:the_end
sleep 3
> execute in minecraft:the_end if block 204 64 204 minecraft:air run say SQ-MELT-24-on_setblock_refused
> execute in minecraft:the_end if block 206 64 206 minecraft:air run say SQ-MELT-24-on_flint_refused
> execute in minecraft:the_end if block 210 64 210 minecraft:soul_fire run say SQ-MELT-24-on_soulfire_kept
expect Could not set the block
expect SQ-MELT-24-on_setblock_refused$
expect SQ-MELT-24-on_flint_refused$
expect SQ-MELT-24-on_soulfire_kept$
> execute in minecraft:the_end run forceload remove 200 200 215 215
edit python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py" toml config/creativecompat-common.toml melting endNoFire false
restart
shell grep -nE "^[[:space:]]*endNoFire = false" config/creativecompat-common.toml
> execute in minecraft:the_end run forceload add 200 200 215 215
sleep 5
> execute in minecraft:the_end run gamerule doFireTick false
> execute in minecraft:the_end run setblock 204 64 204 minecraft:fire
> cdevtest use 208 63 206 held=minecraft:flint_and_steel face=up dim=minecraft:the_end
sleep 3
> execute in minecraft:the_end if block 204 64 204 minecraft:fire run say SQ-MELT-24-off_setblock_fire
> execute in minecraft:the_end if block 208 64 206 minecraft:fire run say SQ-MELT-24-off_flint_fire
expect SQ-MELT-24-off_setblock_fire$
expect SQ-MELT-24-off_flint_fire$
> execute in minecraft:the_end run fill 200 64 200 215 64 215 minecraft:air
> execute in minecraft:the_end run forceload remove 200 200 215 215
edit python3 "$INST/tools/scratch_query/qrun.py" toml config/creativecompat-common.toml melting endNoFire true
restart
look endNoFire true: setblock refused, flint and steel placed nothing, soul fire kept; false: both fires placed; sound by hand only (not judged here)
## CQ-MELT-02 | Saltable tooltip under the Compat lang key
@group client
@commands hover salt blocks and ice items with Compat installed
@pass the gray "Saltable" line shows on saltable items (text, not the raw key `creativecompat.tooltip.saltable`)
@fails `SaltableTooltip` in `creativecompat/melting/`; lang key in Compat's en_us.json
@sources development/creativeCompat/src/main/java/com/SaintAlfonzo/creativecompat/melting/SaltableTooltip.java development/creativeCompat/src/main/resources/assets/creativecompat/lang/en_us.json
# r1124gate (2026-11-24, runner-4): capture driver (client_capture.md 2.11), single player or joined; items from the
# saltable tag (2026-11-19 dump); blue ice, permafrost and the salt block itself are not saltable.
do {"tooltip_text": "minecraft:ice", "expect": "Saltable", "reject": "creativecompat\\.tooltip"}
do {"tooltip_text": "minecraft:packed_ice", "expect": "Saltable", "reject": "creativecompat\\.tooltip"}
do {"tooltip_text": "minecraft:snow_block", "expect": "Saltable", "reject": "creativecompat\\.tooltip"}
do {"tooltip_text": "immersive_weathering:snowy_stone_bricks", "expect": "Saltable", "reject": "creativecompat\\.tooltip"}
do {"tooltip_text": "immersive_weathering:frosty_glass", "expect": "Saltable", "reject": "creativecompat\\.tooltip"}
do {"tooltip_text": "architects_palette:polished_packed_ice", "expect": "Saltable", "reject": "creativecompat\\.tooltip"}
do {"tooltip_text": "minecraft:blue_ice", "reject": "Saltable|creativecompat\\.tooltip"}
do {"tooltip_text": "immersive_weathering:permafrost", "reject": "Saltable|creativecompat\\.tooltip"}
do {"tooltip_text": "salt:salt_block", "reject": "Saltable|creativecompat\\.tooltip"}
> give @s minecraft:ice
do {"screen": "inventory"}
shot saltable_ice_inventory
look the driver steps passed (text "Saltable" on six saltable items, none on blue ice, permafrost, salt block); the shot shows the line gray under the name when hovered
